More useful in practice is predicting the survival curve for specific covariate values. First we
build a small frame of the subjects we want predictions for: a 50-year-old with `sex` 1 and a
70-year-old with `sex` 2. Showing it confirms the covariate values before we predict from them.

::: {#781e3d3e .cell execution_count=14}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import pandas as pd

# Two new subjects: a 50-year-old male and a 70-year-old female
newdata = pd.DataFrame({"age": [50, 70], "sex": [1, 2]})

# Preview the covariate frame before predicting
newdata
