You can also predict conditional on a subject having already survived some time, which is useful for
updating a prognosis partway through follow-up. With `conditional_after=180`, the returned
probabilities are $P(T > t \mid T > 180) = S(t) / S(180)$.

::: {#2673c1c5 .cell execution_count=17}
``` {.python .cell-code}
# Predict P(T > t | T > 180): survival conditional on being alive at day 180
cox.predict(newdata, type="survival", times=[365, 730], conditional_after=180, format="polars")
```

