The result is a single-row frame with one column per subject. When the survival curve never drops
below 0.5 (heavy censoring or low risk), the median is `NaN`.

With `ci=True`, confidence intervals are obtained by inverting the pointwise confidence bands of the
survival curve. The lower bound of the median comes from the lower survival band, and the upper
bound from the upper survival band.

::: {#8c5a28e0 .cell execution_count=19}
``` {.python .cell-code}
# Median survival with confidence intervals
cox.predict_median(newdata, ci=True, format="polars")
```

