### Survival quantiles

`predict_median()` is really a special case of `predict_quantile()`, which generalizes the same
inversion to any set of failure probabilities. Pass a list of values in `(0, 1)` via `p=` to get the
predicted survival time at each quantile, one column per subject.

::: {#64475e5b .cell execution_count=20}
``` {.python .cell-code}
# Predicted survival-time quantiles at the 25th, 50th, and 75th percentiles
cox.predict_quantile(newdata, p=[0.25, 0.5, 0.75], format="polars")
```

